WEBVTT

NOTE CineReels — prov-reelshort-6ae152bbbf9d11c475011619 — Episode 9 — English subtitles
NOTE Transcribed 2026-11-26 from the real episode audio (faster-whisper small).

1
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.160
Who the hell does he think he is turning his phone off?

2
00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:20.930
He sits at home all damn day.

3
00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:24.930
But the second I actually need him, he's nowhere to be found.

4
00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.430
Let me call him. We let him get away with way too much.

5
00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:30.130
He's probably just feeling left out, throwing a fit.

6
00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.430
You even got him a gift, and this is how he acts?

7
00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:34.430
The guy has zero gratitude.

8
00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:35.830
Divorce him!

9
00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:37.430
Kick him out of this family!

10
00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:38.930
Let's see how he survives!

11
00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:41.430
He'll probably end up living out of his car!

12
00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:44.740
Mommy, can we go home?

13
00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:46.240
I'm tired.

14
00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:49.340
Whatever. Let's just wait.

15
00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:51.840
He's probably just tied up with dinner and missed the call.

16
00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:56.340
He better be cooking. Living off us for years, and now he won't even pick up.

17
00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.340
Alira, you're way too soft on him.

18
00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:00.340
Cal, what are you doing here?

19
00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:02.840
In that suit. Where did you get that suit?

20
00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:05.340
You don't even have a job. You can't afford something like that.

21
00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:08.340
Probably rented. Or worse.

22
00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:12.340
Let me guess, Cal. You stole money from the house, didn't you?

23
00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.340
Dressed up just to play the victim?

24
00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.840
Mr. Sterling?

25
00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:19.580
Excuse me, but this bill isn't mine to pay.

26
00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:23.080
Why the hell is it so much?

27
00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:30.880
Alright, Cal. Stop being dramatic.

28
00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:32.880
Here. I got you a gift.

29
00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:37.290
A gift?

30
00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:39.290
You bought Chase a luxury watch.

31
00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:41.790
You won the biggest piece at the auction for him.

32
00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:43.790
And for me? A dying flower?

33
00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:47.790
Alira, that's so generous of you.

34
00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:49.790
Chase is worth the money. And you?

35
00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:52.790
What have you ever done to deserve a dime from us?

36
00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:54.790
She picked it out herself.

37
00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:56.790
Said it suits me perfectly.

38
00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:58.790
Don't be so bitter, Cal.

39
00:01:58.790 --> 00:02:01.790
Thank you. It's so nice of you to actually think of me.

40
00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:03.790
It's just a little something.

41
00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.790
Stop making a scene. Let's go home.

42
00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:07.790
Then I have a gift for you, too.

43
00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:09.790
You got me a gift?
